       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO three times daily, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. Single doses are normally 500\u20131,000 mg, and up to 850 mg with meals when dosed TID.\n- **Risk:** The ordered amount is about twice the maximum daily dose. That raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,700 mg total per day, divided, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- Another dose\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you want, tell me and add a note on the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably want to verify it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
      }
